# Late-copied freeze consumers must rebind final helper identity.
id:                     E2173-draft-2301
trigger_tool:           freeze-generator|receiver|controller|result-validator|bundle-renderer
phase:                  freeze-generation,input-extraction,prepare,launch,result-validation
error_signature:        'EXPECTED_.*HELPER_(?:BYTES|SHA256).*drift|receipt helper.*identity drift|SCHEMA=.*predecessor|input-extract failed rc=1'
severity:               2
category:               freeze|identity|generation_order|receiver|transaction
match_keywords:         late copy, owning render block, helper bytes, helper sha256, schema consumer, generation order, create-new successor
root_cause:             A pipeline rebound the final helper and an early controller consumer, then copied or
                        rendered another receiver, launcher, validator, or fixture from a predecessor after
                        that rebind. The late consumer retained old bytes, SHA-256, or schema constants even
                        though the outer freeze and root helper were current.
affected_scope:         Multi-stage device, CI, or packaging generators in which helper producers and identity
                        consumers are copied or rendered at different points in the generation order.
verification_cmd:       require current helper bytes/SHA/schema in every generated consumer; reject predecessor tuple; independently extract freeze; run exact target transaction
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           owning-render-block-consumer-closure
rec_description:        Enumerate the complete identity-consumer graph, including consumers created after the
                        main rebind. Put bytes, SHA-256, and schema binding in each consumer's owning render
                        block. Require the current tuple exactly once and reject predecessor tuples. Regenerate
                        a create-new freeze and validate it independently before one exact target run.
rec_command:            'bind helper tuple at each owning render block; assert current positive and predecessor negative; regenerate create-new freeze'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               generation
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      final-generated-consumer-verification
fallback_description:   When the generator cannot be refactored immediately, verify every final generated
                        consumer after all copies complete and fail before archive creation on any stale tuple.
fallback_command:       Inspect final generated consumers, then create a new archive only when all identities match.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          validation
forbid_1_pattern:       patch.*(?:completed|consumed).*(?:freeze|bundle|archive)
forbid_1_reason:         Editing completed evidence destroys the identity of the failed generation.
forbid_1_consequence:   A later target result can no longer be attributed to a create-new immutable input.
forbid_2_pattern:       accept.*(?:old|new).*(?:schema|sha|bytes)
forbid_2_reason:         Accepting multiple identities weakens exact package and transaction attribution.
forbid_2_consequence:   A predecessor helper can be executed under a current outer manifest.
principles:             P007, P018, P020
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
doc_file:               drafts/E2173-draft-2301.md
last_updated:           2026-08-27
source_event:           GLib 2.88.3 r870 root-schema drift, r872 receiver helper bytes/SHA drift, and r873 same-snapshot W3 PASS
